            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0764" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 894.607 A/230.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Department of Foreign Affairs to the
                        Japanese Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Imperial Japanese Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>. (<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1912-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Undated</hi></date>.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Left by the Ambassador at the Department of State, March 6,
                    1912.]</p>
                <p>On submitting the question of the proposed exhibition in 1917 to a new
                    examination and considering all the surrounding circumstances and the advantages
                    as well as disadvantages of holding such an exhibition in Japan at the time
                    appointed, the Imperial Government have persuaded themselves of the inexpediency
                    of carrying out the project. They have accordingly decided, with much reluctance
                    and deep regret, to abandon the scheme. You are instructed to bring the decision
                    to the attention of the United States Government and at the same time express to
                    the Secretary of State the sense of high appreciation on the part of the
                    Imperial Government of the very friendly encouragement and generous support
                    which the Government of the United States had given to the undertaking.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
